message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "MoneroVM: Optimistic RandomX Execution Verification via Fraud Proofs on Starknet"
authors:
  - family-names: "Espejel"
    given-names: "Omar"
    affiliation: "Starknet Foundation"
date-released: "2025-12-04"
url: "https://github.com/omarespejel/monero-vm"
repository-code: "https://github.com/omarespejel/monero-vm"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - monero
  - starknet
  - fraud-proofs
  - randomx
  - cairo
  - bisection-protocol
  - optimistic-verification
abstract: >-
  MoneroVM implements an optimistic fraud proof system for verifying
  RandomX proof-of-work computations on Starknet. It uses a bisection
  protocol with ERC20 bond enforcement to enable trustless Monero
  block validation disputes. Part of the Monero-Starknet Atomic Swap
  system.
